    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "1933135213690798343",
      "url": "https://x.com/BRPSierraMadre/status/1933135213690798343",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/BRPSierraMadre/status/1933135213690798343",
      "text": "Grounding a Militia Ship Near Pagasa Is No Accident—It’s a Provocation in Disguise\n\nChina’s so-called “stranded” vessel near Pagasa Island isn’t about rough seas—it’s a calculated move, a grey-zone tactic disguised as an accident. It’s about normalizing intrusion, testing the Philippines’ response, and expanding control without triggering open conflict.\n\nThis wasn’t a navigational error. It’s Beijing’s signature maneuver: use state-backed militia ships to blur lines between civilians and military assets—spy vessels, intimidation tools, and political weapons rolled into one.\n\nAnd no—this is not like the Philippines’ 1999 BRP Sierra Madre grounding. That was a lawful move within our Exclusive Economic Zone, backed by UNCLOS and the 2016 Arbitral Ruling. What #China is doing now is illegal trespassing in waters it has no right to claim.\n\nGrounding a vessel just one nautical mile from Pagasa sends a dangerous message: “We can move in—and stay.” It’s part of China’s “control by presence” playbook—a creeping campaign to redefine sovereignty by proximity.\n\nThis isn’t miscalculation—it’s manipulation. Not diplomacy—it’s deception. If we treat this as routine, the next grounding could be permanent occupation.\n\nThe #Philippines must act with clarity and resolve: expose this tactic, reassert international law, and prepare for the next phase of escalation.\n\nThe law is clear. The ruling is final. The aggression is escalating.\nBeijing’s playbook is in motion—and we know where it leads.\n#StandWithPagasa #GreyZoneAggression #SouthChinaSeaTruth #ChinaIsTheAggressor #UNCLOS #DefendWestPHSea #MaritimeFreedomNow #ExposeCCPDeception #SouthChinaSea #WestPhilippineSea",
